<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb industrial output falls 3.4 pct mth/mth. [CORRECTED 5:07 GMT]</title>
<headline>Japan Feb industrial output falls 3.4 pct mth/mth. [CORRECTED 5:07 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's industrial production in February fell a preliminary 3.4 percent from the previous month on a seasonally adjusted basis, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Friday.</p>
<p>MITI said in a statement that industrial output was on an upward trend.</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted month-on-month (pct), index base 1990:</p>
<p>				  FEB	MONTH AGO     FEB INDEX</p>
<p> Output			 -3.4	+5.6	 102.2</p>
<p> Shipments		    -4.0	+6.4	 104.4</p>
<p> Inventories		  -0.7	 0.0	 106.2</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>    Shipments ratio	 +0.5	-3.5	 108.3</p>
<p>Unadjusted year-on-year (pct) (corrects figures for February):</p>
<p>				  FEB	MONTH AGO</p>
<p> Output			 +3.4	+8.9</p>
<p> Shipments		    +4.3     +10.8</p>
<p> Inventories		  -3.4	-2.5</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>    Shipments ratio	-5.2	-9.0</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of MITI's forecasts for manufacturers' output:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted, month-on-month (in pct):</p>
<p>		     MAR forecast   APR forecast</p>
<p>		     -2.0	     +1.0</p>
</text>
